  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Environmental and Social Scoping Study for Flyling Swans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands and Kenya are important partners in the production and trade of horticulture products. This project serves multiple objectives of a signed Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the two countries, amongst others concerning the transport of perishables, transitioning from air-freight to sea-freight export and related necessity for expanded cold chain infrastructure.Further development of sustainable and future proof perishables export from Kenya could have mutual benefits concerning job creation, strengthening the hub position of both countries and creation of value chains that are more climate resilient and socially sustainable.This project will produce a Strategic Environmental and Social Scoping Study that will provide insights for the development of the Cool Logistics Corridor on environmental, social and climate risks.</narrative>
  </description>
